Pre-purification, regeneration and contaminant accumulation (@gas-prepurification: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @industrial-gases-and-vacuum, #source "../sources/Cryogenic-Air-Separation-EIGA.lingua#r_39BST0TM9XV9VEZ14NXVJW7TWA", #source "../sources/Adsorption-Science-and-Technology-Mondal.lingua#r_4P0F5BH9XEAJQPGJ0CTTJ76XM5", #industrial-gases-and-vacuum "Argon-and-the-value-of-coupled-product-recovery.lingua#r_5XGQ4X72J3BKJBVXSKDWSRX9V9") { r_32Z6YZ0SRCWX9CS1K2DBZWZQ2H
**Read:** [Guideline for Safe Practices for Cryogenic Air Separation Plants — EIGA 147/22](../sources/Cryogenic-Air-Separation-EIGA.lingua#r_39BST0TM9XV9VEZ14NXVJW7TWA), chapter 9 in full; [Adsorption Science and Technology — Sourav Mondal, IIT Kharagpur](../sources/Adsorption-Science-and-Technology-Mondal.lingua#r_4P0F5BH9XEAJQPGJ0CTTJ76XM5), equilibrium, kinetics and fixed beds; the shared gas-separation chemistry.

A pre-purification system must remove contaminants across the intended feed variation and service interval. An adsorbent's equilibrium capacity alone does not determine when the outlet concentration rises: transport, heat release, competition and flow distribution matter. Regeneration changes the next cycle's initial state.

Trace components can pass one treatment and accumulate elsewhere. Follow both the useful gas and each consequential impurity through purge, drains, recycles and product streams. A stationary total flow can coexist with a slowly increasing contaminant inventory. Changing a regeneration gas can transfer impurities between systems.

**Work:** Write transient constituent balances for a two-bed arrangement with one bed adsorbing and the other regenerating. Identify the observations needed to estimate working capacity and residual loading. Construct a case where average feed quality is acceptable but a transient contaminant pulse changes the next cycle. Keep numerical limits tied to actual equipment and evidence.

**Return:** [Industrial gases, vacuum and high-purity supplies](../Industrial-gases-and-vacuum.lingua#r_3GHQJEYMYEN6JDKSF4PPJ403RF).
**Continue in gas and vacuum systems:** [Argon and the value of coupled product recovery](Argon-and-the-value-of-coupled-product-recovery.lingua#r_5XGQ4X72J3BKJBVXSKDWSRX9V9).

